---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { href } from "../lib";
import { breadcrumbs } from "../schema";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Leat Consulting is a UK-based platform engineering consultancy founded by Fraser Davidson, a platform engineer with over twelve years in large, regulated organisations."
  schema={[breadcrumbs([{ name: "About", path: "about/" }])]}
>
  <section class="band band--hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
    <h1>Founder-led, built on twelve years of platform work</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Leat Consulting is a UK-based platform engineering consultancy, founded by Fraser Davidson, a platform
      engineer with over twelve years in the industry, most of them inside large, regulated organisations: tier 1 banks, financial technology and
      trading firms, global enterprises and the public sector.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
    <h2 id="experience-heading">Experience</h2>
    <p>
      That work has centred on the systems that build and run software: multi-account AWS estates, GitLab and
      GitHub pipelines, Terraform and Kubernetes, and the security that holds them together, from short-lived
      cloud credentials to delivery that stands up to an audit.
    </p>
    <p>Leat brings that standard to teams that want it without building a platform team to get it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--tint" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
    <h2 id="work-heading">How we work</h2>
    <ul class="ticks">
      <li>We show our own work. Our pipelines and the rules that protect them are public.</li>
      <li>We work through pull and merge requests in your repositories, so your team sees and approves every change.</li>
      <li>We hand over. You own what we deliver, and your team can run it without us.</li>
      <li>We are plain about trade-offs, including when the simpler option is the right one.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={href("contact/")}>Talk to us</a></div>
  </section>
</Base>
